        "opacity": 1.0
      },
      "meta": {
        "author": "human",
        "text": "The Physics of UHI\nUrban areas are significantly warmer than surrounding rural areas. This is primarily due to Albedo (the reflectivity of surfaces) and Thermal Mass. Dark surfaces like asphalt have low albedo, absorbing up to 90% of solar radiation. Meanwhile, materials like concrete act as a \"Heat Battery,\" storing energy during the day and releasing it at night.",
        "summary": "",
        "role": "body",
        "fontFamily": "sans-serif",
        "fontWeight": "400",
        "fontSize": 18,
        "growDir": "right-down",
        "baseWidth": 604.8046875000001,
        "baseHeight": 314.16234375000005,
        "configuredWidth": 604.8046875000001,
        "configuredHeight": 314.16234375000005,
        "lineHeight": 1.4,
        "padding": 0,
        "contentWidth": 436.7031860351563,
        "contentHeight": 226.79999999999998,
        "lineCount": 9,
        "renderedText": "The Physics of UHI\nUrban areas are significantly warmer than\nsurrounding rural areas. This is primarily due to\nAlbedo (the reflectivity of surfaces) and Thermal\nMass. Dark surfaces like asphalt have low albedo,\nabsorbing up to 90% of solar radiation. Meanwhile,\nmaterials like concrete act as a \"Heat Battery,\"\nstoring energy during the day and releasing it at\nnight."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "text_mmulzgrp_5d07",
      "tool": "text",
      "points": [
